{"id": "Dbx6-3KhhEh", "title": "Video by krishnachaytanyaa", "description": "Serverless cold starts explained: why the same function takes 1,180ms for one request and 40ms for the next.\nYour function is not running until someone calls it. When traffic grows past what is already warm, the platform has to build a NEW execution environment first: fetch your code, start the runtime, run your init. That is the cold start, and whoever landed on that one waits through all of it.\nEveryone after them goes straight in. Then the traffic stops, the platform tears it down, and the next person pays again.\nCold starts are NOT just the first request. Every scale out past what is already warm pays one.\nHave you been hit by this in production, on Lambda, Vercel, Cloud Run or Azure Functions? Save this for the next time someone asks why your API is randomly slow.\nFollow @krishnachaytanyaa for backend and system design concepts you can actually see.\n#serverless #coldstart #awslambda #systemdesign #backend", "timestamp": 1786194007, "channel": "krishnachaytanyaa", "uploader": "Krishna Chaitanya | Solutions Architect", "uploader_id": "27131031756", "like_count": 913, "comment_count": 4, "http_headers": {"Referer": "https://www.instagram.com/"}, "duration": 9.006999969482422, "formats": [{"format_id": "dash-1729978571274544a", "ext": "m4a", "tbr": 48.175, "asr": 44100, "format_note": "DASH audio", "container": "m4a_dash", "vcodec": "none", "acodec": "mp4a.40.5", "url": "https://instagram.fblr20-4.fna.fbcdn.net/o1/v/t2/f2/m78/AQO3ghE9GN0UATscSyTw4NAghNQ6o7wOH1RYgRkKjZ8A_Hmfj_xDl3S0aNyFUpFfVjcyLIrKZTstmnlZqG1UiyvXkFk5Rt_IbJM_KvQ.mp4?_nc_cat=106&_nc_oc=AdqmtwlVFZ38D-nEfrFc3ggMsbdUrii-aw5OzjSINkofQpfILCSdIZFXF9AgXXhlsV7Q9Tj0XUNZbizBf2yUrtkS&_nc_sid=9ca052&_nc_ht=instagram.fblr20-4.fna.fbcdn.net&_nc_ohc=dsnGiTd22fsQ7kNvwFu86bQ&%3D&ccb=17-1&_nc_gid=HyWYsUqR94Z03lOBo7L9qA&_nc_ss=7a22e&_nc_zt=28&oh=00_AQFAeVHBnNiJg1aCr1sEdDnsKGu8FX7D1KTrSpL_LfOU2w&oe=6A834C9B", "manifest_stream_number": 0, 